    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0091",
      "sequence": 103,
      "meaning": "They tell the mountain king the whole affair. He grieves on hearing of Kāma’s burning but rejoices greatly when they recount Rati’s boon. Reflecting upon Śambhu’s majesty, Himālaya respectfully summons eminent astrologer-sages, has them calculate a favorable day, constellation and hour, and quickly fix the Vedic wedding moment. He gives the letter to the Seven Sages and pleads at their feet. They deliver it to Brahmā, whose heart overflows with love as he reads it; he announces the wedding time to all. Sages and gods rejoice, flowers rain from the sky, instruments sound, auspicious vessels adorn all ten directions, the gods prepare mounts and aircraft, favorable omens arise and apsarases sing.",
