    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0093",
      "sequence": 105,
      "meaning": "Viṣṇu warns that a procession should resemble its groom, lest they be mocked in another city. Smiling, the gods separate with their armies. Maheśa smiles inwardly, recognizing that Hari’s discerning words never fail. Hearing these dear words from his beloved friend, he sends Bhṛṅgī to summon every attendant. They obey Śiva’s command, arrive and bow at his lotus feet. Seeing his own strange company in varied guises and on varied mounts, Śiva laughs: some lack faces while others have many; some lack feet or hands while others have many legs and arms; some possess countless eyes while others have none, and some are immensely stout while others extremely thin.",
