    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0095",
      "sequence": 107,
      "meaning": "News reaches the city that the wedding party is near, increasing its commotion and beauty. Citizens dress splendidly, decorate many vehicles and go respectfully to receive it. They rejoice on seeing the gods’ army and delight especially in Hari, but when they behold Śiva’s company their mounts bolt and flee. Only the mature stand firm; children run away, clinging to life. Reaching home, they answer their parents with trembling bodies: the sight cannot be described—was it Yama’s host or a wedding procession? The groom is mad, riding a bull, adorned with serpents, skulls and ash.",
